          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A pickleball court is 20 by 44 feet, measured to the outside of the 2-inch lines, with a 7-foot kitchen on each side of a net that stands 36 inches at the sidelines and 34 inches at the centre. The same court serves singles and doubles.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Leave room around it, ideally the rulebook's 30 by 60 foot minimum playing surface, square the rectangle by checking the diagonals, and keep the kitchen and net height exact even on a shortened home court. Those details matter more than any other part of the layout.
